      "value": "What we need to finalise user stories per epic\n----------------------------------------------\n\nPWA Kit user stories cannot be written, reviewed or signed off until the relevant design components are locked. Here is what that means in practice.\n\n### 1 — Components must be finalised first\n\n* Before user stories can be written for an epic e.g. Checkout Flow & Delivery, **every UI component that appears in that epic must be finalised in the UI kit** — fully componentised in Figma with all variations, states and responsive sizes accounted for. This allows us to build the component user story.\n* Each component is owned by the **earliest epic in the sequence where it appears**. That epic is responsible for designing all variations of that component — including any variations needed by later epics. For example, if a product card component appears on PDP, PLP and Homepage, all three variations must be designed and locked as part of the PDP.\n\n> As we move through the epic sequence, design effort should reduce. By the time we reach epics like Homepage or Wishlist, most components should already exist. Design at that stage should be limited to anything genuinely net-new.\n\n### 2 — Design freeze\n\n* **Hard rule:** Once a component is finalised and added to the UI kit, **it is locked — no further UX or design changes are permitted**. User stories are written against locked designs only. Any change after lock requires a formal review of every story and epic that references that component.\n\n### 3 — Sign-off checklist per epic\n\n* Before component user stories are submitted for PO review, confirm the component has ALL variations included in the UI kit.\n\n---\n\nComponent Design & User Story Tracker\n-------------------------------------\n\n| Epic | Example Design scope | Design components finalised | User stories ready for PO review | User stories ready for development | Design & user story sprint(s) | BA lead | Design lead |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- 